{{nihongo|'''Yodohime jinja'''|與止日女神社|}}, also known as the '''Kawakami jinja''', is a [[Japan]]ese [[Shinto shrine]] in [[Kawakami, Saga|Kawakami]], [[Saga Prefecture]]. 

==History==
''Yodohime jinja'' was founded in the sixth century. It enshrines the ''[[kami]]'' of the grandmother of [[Emperor Jimmu]]. 

It was one of two chief [[Shinto shrine]] (''ichinomiya'') of [[Hizen Province]] and Saga Prefecture.<ref>Picken, Stuart. (2004). [http://books.google.com/books?id=v7Xs1NzMMHMC&pg=PA377&lpg=PA377&dq=   ''Sourcebook in Shinto: Selected Documents,'' p. 377]; [http://eos.kokugakuin.ac.jp/modules/xwords/images/uploads/EOS070712Ab.pdf "Nationwide List of ''Ichinomiya''," p. 3]; retrieved 2012-8-23.</ref>

